      "problem": "Use the first three terms of the binomial expansion of $(3+x)^{5}$ in ascending powers of $x$ to approximate $(2.96)^{5}.$ Give your answer to three decimal places.",
      "worked_solution": "The binomial theorem for positive integer $n$ states that\n\n$$\n(a+b)^{n}=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{0}){a}^{n}{b}^{0}+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{1}){a}^{n-1}{b}^{1}+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{2}){a}^{n-2}{b}^{2}+\u2026+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{n}){a}^{0}{b}^{n}.\n$$\n\nBy substituting $a=3,$ $b=x,$ and $n=5,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(3+x)}^{5} & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{0}){(3)}^{5}{(x)}^{0}+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{1}){(3)}^{5-1}{(x)}^{1}+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{2}){(3)}^{5-2}{(x)}^{2}+\u22ef \\\\  & =1{(3)}^{5}+5{(3)}^{4}{(x)}^{1}+10{(3)}^{3}{(x)}^{2}+\u22ef \\\\  & =243+5(81)(x)+10(27)({x}^{2})+\u22ef \\\\  & =243+405x+270{x}^{2}+\u22ef\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, for small $x,$ we have\n\n$$\n{(3+x)}^{5}\u2248243+405x+270{x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $x=-0.04$ into the above approximation of $(3+x)^{5}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2.96)^{5} & =(3+(-0.04))^{5} \\\\  & \u2248243+405(-0.04)+270(-0.04)^{2} \\\\  & =243-405(0.04)+270(0.001\\,6) \\\\  & =243-16.2+0.432 \\\\  & =227.232,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nto three decimal places.",
